## Impact
In `V3Vault::liquidate`, the borrower can liquidate his/her own position. The borrower's obligation is to pay debts and interests while a liquidator's business is to liquidate positions that are deemed unhealthy. The borrower should have no business in liquidations even if it is his/her own debt position.

This is what will happen if left unfixed:
    - The liquidators will be forced to compete with the borrowers for liquidation profit. And since the borrowers know their own debt positions best, chances are the borrowers will reap the liquidation profit. Soon enough, liquidators will be demotivated in liquidating the protocol's unhealthy debt positions.
    - There is a lurking risk where the borrowers might game the system.

