The following code is used to send leftover tokens back to the user at the end of executing within `AutoExit.execute()`:

```solidity
state.owner = nonfungiblePositionManager.ownerOf(params.tokenId);
if (state.amount0 > 0) {
    _transferToken(state.owner, IERC20(state.token0), state.amount0, true); //@audit so these get transferred to vault
}
if (state.amount1 > 0) {
    _transferToken(state.owner, IERC20(state.token1), state.amount1, true);
}
```

The issue is that the Revert Lend Vault may be the owner of the position, so the leftovers are sent to the vault rather than the true owner of the position.
This leads to loss of funds for the user, and also is a DoS if one of the tokens happened to be WETH.

## Impact
As the leftover tokens would be transferred to the Vault when the position is exited, the user's funds are lost.

Even worse: If one of the tokens was WETH, it is unwrapped into ether before being sent into the vault. Since the vault doesn't have logic to accept ether, this attempted transfer will fail, leading to a revert. So the AutoExit will not be able to be executed as the position owner intends, making the AutoExit extremely unreliable.

